  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 231 AM EDT Monday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Another day of cool and showery weather is expected \nacross the region today as additional rounds of showers move through \nthe region as the system to our south slowly drifts eastward. \nGreatest rainfall amounts for today are expected across eastern and \nsouthern Vermont, where totals are expected to be between 0.25 and \n0.5 inches of rain, while northern New York looks to remain on the \ndrier side. The showers and cloud cover will keep temperatures on \nthe cool side for this time of year, with highs only climbing into \nthe upper 50s and low 60s. \n\nShower activity will gradually wane through the evening and \novernight hours tonight as the low shifts away, with drier weather \nconditions expected to prevail throughout much of the day Tuesday as \nhigh pressure begins to build into the region. The drier conditions \nare expected to continue through much of the week, with temperatures \ngradually trending warmer as well. High temperatures on Tuesday will \nonly be in the 50s and lower 60s again, but by Thursday widespread \nhighs in the 70s are expected.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: A cold front will make its way southward across our \nregion late Thursday into Friday, bringing increasing chances of \nprecipitation along with it. The best forcing will remain well to \nour north, so anticipate scattered to perhaps widespread showers, \nmostly light to occasionally moderate in nature. Thunder is not \nanticipated given the unfavorable timing of the frontal passage \n(overnight Thu into early Fri AM). High pressure will immediately \nfollow the front, ushering in a drier and cooler airmass for at \nleast the first half of the weekend. Sunday is a bit less certain; \nthe 00z GFS and to a lesser extent, the 00z CMC indicate a wave of \nprecipitation lifting into our region sometime Sunday. The \ndeterministic GFS is the most aggressive with this feature, though \nit does the support of a few of its ensemble members, along with \nsome GEPS members, as well. Didn't get a chance to look at the 00z \nECMWF, but the 12z run held off any precipitation until Sunday \nnight/Monday, though again, some of its ensemble members show a \nrainy and cool Sunday. Given these differences, have stayed with the \nWPC/NBM forecast, which gives low chance PoPs for Sunday. \nTemperatures will be warmest on Friday, in the mid 60s to near 70F, \nthen trending cooler with highs in the 60s and lows in the low 30s \nto low 40s.",
